The prompt’s task is a frequency histogram over space-separated letters. I’m using a straightforward two-pass implementation: count every token, track the maximum, then retain exactly the keys at that maximum. This keeps the Python implementation independently executable while limiting the semantics to ordinary functions, assignments, conditionals, loops, calls, comparisons, and dictionaries.
