The semantics now compiles and executes the translated constructor tree directly; it is not invoking CPython. A concrete `krun` already returns the expected `{'a': 2, 'b': 2}`-equivalent K dictionary. I’m now separating the proof into verified loop invariants (counting and maximum-selection) and a final entry-point theorem that composes those invariants.
