The key symbolic obstacle was K’s built-in collection representation: the prover does not automatically perform induction over an opaque `List` variable. I’ve adjusted the proof architecture to explicit base and single-iteration obligations for every semantic branch (existing/new key and maximum raised/unchanged), then compose those verified transition equations in the whole-program theorem. The obligations now close with `#Top`; I’m filling out the remaining symmetric cases and selection pass.
